  "implementation": [
    "The trigger-aware outer executor collects affected FK relationships using the existing compiler over actual reachable program statements. Internal body/base calls retain the live foreign_keys setting and accumulate the actual accepted-row write ledger. Immediate NO ACTION validation runs against the full before/after database at the outer boundary, before any publication; the caller ledger is restored afterward. Ordinary trigger-free statements keep their original boundary.",
    "Captured UPDATE resolves every target and prepares every original expression, then evaluates only the last assignment to each actual column position. Integer-primary-key and implicit-rowid aliases share that position. Earlier invalid function names still fail preparation, while earlier valid but overflowing runtime expressions are not evaluated.",
    "A compiler context marks actual VIEW/trigger reads. Only resolved PRAGMA virtual-table execution enforces DIRECTONLY; physical tables with the same spelling remain ordinary sources, and JSON table functions remain admitted. Private view materialization restores the caller context, and trigger-frame restoration preserves it. The ordinary pragma_foreign_keys read source exposes the actual live setting outside schema programs."
  ],
  "reference_protocol": "Both public file modes compare complete stdout/exit/first-error and independently read persisted tables/catalog/integrity against pinned SQLite 3.53.4. Sixteen randomized parent-repair programs use fresh final values. Negative FK outcomes and direct-only errors remain ordinary reference comparisons, with no skips, expected-failure escape or oracle route.",
  "crash_scope": "Fresh rerun of the retained 204 SIGKILL timing samples, including actual AFTER-trigger writes to two tables and an index. Production Lean recovery is observed independently with SQLite. These are finite process-crash samples, not exhaustive power-loss/syscall schedules.",
  "primary_source_basis": "Pinned fkey.c immediate NO ACTION counters and trigger statements share the outer VDBE completion boundary; pragma.c virtual-table DIRECTONLY registration; update.c assignment-column map. Boundary outcomes are checked independently by the pinned native reference.",
  "proof_scope": "Existing CoreForeignKey.requireTransition_clause remains unchanged and guards the real outer before/after boundary. New audited component contracts cover empty effective assignments, caller schema-context restoration and resolved PRAGMA schema-program rejection. All retained Core/physical/file contracts compile. No whole-trigger/SQL equivalence theorem is claimed.",
  "limitations": [
    "BEFORE/INSTEAD OF/temporary triggers, RAISE, recursive_triggers settings, triggered UPSERT, ALTER and wider trigger constraints remain. FK action/deferred declarations beyond the already admitted immediate NO ACTION slice remain unsupported.",
    "WITHOUT ROWID, composite primary keys and partial/expression indexes still account for eight failures in the 88 named probes. Those probes are not a global coverage denominator.",
    "UTF-16 writes/setters, native-key/materialization limits, pending new physical allocations and earlier SQL/storage limitations remain."
  ],
